  "body": "Found during the work on PR #2985 (issue #2901).\n\n## What happens\n\nThe new refusal for a low first traverse names the clearance height and the height that it must clear. On a 3+2 operation the two values are heights along the tilted tool axis. In the guide example the message says \"clearance height Z10.000\", but the user typed 30 for the clearance height.\n\nThe refusal is correct. The message is misleading: the user cannot find the value \"10\" in the operation.\n\n## What is expected\n\nThe message names the value that the user typed, or it says that the heights are in the frame of the tilted tool. It tells the user how much to raise the clearance height.\n\n## Done when\n\n- A test with a tilted operation pins the new message text.\n- The message has no G-code terms.\n\nRefs #2901\n",
